cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use spaCraft in your research, please cite this software."
title: "spaCraft: calibrated power analysis and sample-size planning for multi-sample spatial transcriptomics"
type: software
version: 1.0.1
date-released: 2026-07-17

authors:
  - family-names: "Shin"
    given-names: "Jungmin"
    email: "c16267@gmail.com"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0006-7471-0437"
  - family-names: "Chung"
    given-names: "Dongjun"
    email: "chung.911@osu.edu"

identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.21907013"

abstract: >-
  spaCraft is a pilot-based framework for statistical power analysis and
  sample-size determination in comparative multi-sample spatial transcriptomics
  studies. It learns a cohort-level generative model for domain composition,
  spatial geometry, and spatially correlated expression, then estimates power
  through an analysis-aware generate-recover-test pipeline that re-discovers
  spatial domains in every synthetic replicate. The framework provides
  spatially adjusted differential-expression and domain-composition endpoints,
  supports replicated and single-pilot designs, and has been evaluated across
  Visium, Visium HD, and Stereo-seq platforms.

repository-code: "https://github.com/c16267/spaCraft"
